# CANFAR lab session layout

- **Code + env:** `${WORK:-/srcdir}` — ephemeral; `git push` or `astroai-lab save` before the session ends.
- **Data + download caches:** `${SCRATCH:-/scratch}` when mounted — session-private.
- **Platform Python CLIs:** `/opt/astroai/venv/cadc` (`canfar`, `cadcget`, `astroai-lab`) — user-writable this session via `upgrade-cadc-tools.sh`.
- **Persistent home:** `/arc` — agent MCP under `~/.cursor`, saves under `~/.astroai/lab`, gh auth.
- **Project deps:** pixi/uv lockfiles under `${WORK}` — prefer `pixi install` / `uv sync`, not ad-hoc image venv edits for app code.
- **Status:** `astroai-lab status --json` for quotas and team projects (access/ACL/GMS/vault); `astroai-lab env export` for resolved session paths; `canfar ps` for sessions.

CLI flags: `--json`, `--yes`, `--dry-run` may appear before or on subcommands (e.g. `astroai-lab agent verify --clean --dry-run`).

Prefer pre-installed CLIs (`rg`, `fd`, `gh`, `bat`, `jq`, `shellcheck`) over MCP when they answer the question with fewer tokens.
